        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Plan on roughly $6 to $12 per square foot for a plain broom-finished concrete patio and roughly $12 to $25 for stamped, with stained and exposed aggregate finishes in between. Small patios cost more per square foot, large ones less, and removal, access, drainage and permits can move the total more than the finish does.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Spend where it counts: a compacted base, proper slope, control joints and air-entrained concrete in cold climates. Let the slab cure properly, seal it once the sealer label says it is ready, and reseal decorative finishes every few years. A patio built that way is one of the best-value outdoor spaces you can add.
          </p>
